      "knowledge_point": "The Period of a Transformed Function",
      "problem": "Calculate the period of the function $y=-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$",
      "worked_solution": "Given a function of the form $y=A\\operatorname{sec}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{(\\frac{1}{2})}=4\\pi .$",
