      "math_academy_id": "e-3858",
      "knowledge_point_id": "0b19d6e0-8a12-525d-8c80-ac2de8080830",
      "knowledge_point": "The Period of a Transformed Function",
      "problem": "What is the period of the function $y = 4\\sec\\left(2x-1\\right)-5?$",
      "worked_solution": "Given a function of the form $y = A\\sec(Bx +C) + D,$ the period is $\\dfrac{2\\pi}{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=2.$ Therefore, the period is $\\dfrac{2\\pi}{2}=\\pi.$",
